    "items": [
      "Changing `DLC1LvlSoulCairnBonemanMissile` 0071AA also needs `DLC1SoulCairnBonemanSummon` 0045B9:Dawnguard.esm and `ccRMSSSE001_BonemanSummon` 000863:ccrmssse001-necrohouse.esl (summons, level 6; on *Undead Summons*): they use 0071AA as their template but not for `Stats`. `DLC1LvlSoulCairnMistman` 0071AF likewise has `DLC1SoulCairnMistmanSummon` 0045B7 and `ccRMSSSE001_MistmanSummon` 000852 (level 13), and `DLC1LvlSoulCairnWrathman` 0071AD has `DLC1SoulCairnWrathmanSummon` 0045B4 and `ccRMSSSE001_WrathmanSummon` 000843 (level 30).",
      "The Keepers use the Common Skeleton records as their templates (BowArrow `EncSkeleton01Melee1H` 02D1DE, Shield `…Melee1Hshield` 02D1FD, 2H `…Melee2H` 02D1E0) but not for `Stats`, so they keep their own levels.",
      "Every Soul carries `Stats`; the records that keep their own level beside the bandit and warlock ladders are on *Common Bandits* and Warlocks → *Necromancers*.",
      "The same-race records with no template are filed elsewhere: the four `EncSkeleton01*` skeletons on *Common Skeletons*; the CC necromancy skeletons on *Undead Summons*; the unused `DLC1SoulCairnEnc*` records on the *Skeletons* group page.",
      "The other rows: no other record keeps its own level."
    ]
  },
